<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/inventions?focus=spear-thrower">Inventions &amp; Discoveries</a> · Weapons and war</p><h1 class="enc-title">Spear-thrower</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as atlatl, woomera, spear-throwing lever</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">A spear-thrower, or atlatl, is a lever, usually about as long as the user's arm or forearm, with a cup or spur that holds the butt of a dart or javelin and throws it faster than the arm alone could. It is believed to have been used by Homo sapiens since the Upper Paleolithic, and the earliest known example is a Solutrean spear-thrower of reindeer antler, 17,500 years old, from Combe Saunière in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dordogne">Dordogne</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a>. Ice Age hunters used it against megafauna; in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/europe">Europe</a> the bow and arrow supplemented it, while it stayed in use in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/americas">Americas</a>, where Teotihuacan's warriors carried it, and in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/australia">Australia</a> as the woomera.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/spear-thrower.jpg" alt="Spear-thrower" width="330" height="176" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Sebastião da Silva Vieira · CC BY 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Nativo_do_Novo_Mundo_lançando_flecha_com_o_propulsor_ou_estólica.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
<section class="inv-entry"><h2 class="enc-section-title">On the inventions tree</h2><dl class="inv-entry-facts"><div><dt>First known</dt><dd>c. 17,500 years ago</dd></div><div><dt>Where</dt><dd>Combe Saunière, Dordogne, France</dd></div></dl><p class="inv-entry-note"><span class="inv-k">Note</span>It may be older: it is believed to have been in use from around 30,000 years ago, and the arthritic right elbow of Mungo Man, of 42,000 BP, has been read as 'atlatl elbow'.</p><p class="enc-article-foot"><a class="enc-random-link" href="/inventions?focus=spear-thrower">See it on the inventions tree &rarr;</a></p></section>
